  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "A refitted sleeper car waits at Vienna's main station. Photograph by Lukas Brandt.",
   "marks": [],
   "places": [
    {
     "kind": "page",
     "start": 0,
     "end": 82,
     "page": 2,
     "left": 0.06045751633986928,
     "top": 0.4027777777777778,
     "width": 0.5424836601307189,
     "height": 0.015151515151515138
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "T he last time Anna Kovac took the sleeper fromVienna to Venice, she was nineteen and the carriages smelled of diesel and oranges. This spring she made the trip again, in a refitted cabin with a reading lamp, a folding desk and a door that locks. Nothing about the route had changed, except that people had once decided to give it up.",
   "marks": [],
   "places": [
    {
     "kind": "page",
     "start": 0,
     "end": 34,
     "page": 2,
