  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Between 2010and 2020 operators across the continent closed more than a dozen overnight routes. Cheap flights had made them look like relics, and replacing the worn rolling stock seemed impossible to justify. Then the arithmetic shifted. Fuel prices climbed, airports grew crowded, and a generation of travellers began to count the carbon in an itinerary as carefully as the euros.",
   "marks": [],
   "places": [
    {
     "kind": "page",
     "start": 0,
     "end": 41,
     "page": 2,
