  {
   "kind": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "What a berth costs",
   "marks": [],
   "places": [
    {
     "kind": "page",
     "start": 0,
     "end": 18,
     "page": 2,
     "left": 0.511437908496732,
     "top": 0.5113636363636364,
     "width": 0.19771241830065367,
     "height": 0.02020202020202022
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "A sleeper berth costs several timeswhat a seat does to run. A carriage that carries sixty people by day carries only twenty-four at night, and it spends the small hours standing in sidingswhile crews rest. Operatorssay a typical overnight train needsa public subsidy of about forty euros for each passenger it carries, roughly the price of the ticket itself.",
